      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Context:\n\"C# allows you to specify a parameter to be an out variable which can then be used to store data that the caller can use. I’ve seen this mostly in physics raycast methods that return a bool, but use the raycasthit as an out variable to store the hit information. The issue I ran into for the car is that wheel colliders use a function with out variables to get the position and rotation of the wheel. Since it returns nothing but only takes in these out variables, it’s useless for us in Udon.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
